-- regenerate it with ./gradlew generate rather than editing it.

---Carousels contain a series of entries, and only display one at a time, allowing the user to switch between them via
---buttons to the left and right of the carousel's contents.
---
---They're ideal for situations where you have a limited set of options that relate to eachother, such as game settings.
---
---Entries can be displayed as either an icon, or as a text label, with support for mixing and matching within the same
---carousel.
---
---Custom Visuals: Using custom or plugin-provided sprites is supported, however the provided sprite must represent a
---spritesheet containing all of the potential states in a vertical layout using the following order - `default`,
---`mouseover`, `pressed`, `disabled`.
---@class ui.Carousel : ui.Component
---@field selectedID integer (Read-only) The numeric ID for the currently selected entry, or -1 if there is no selection.
---@field buttonWidth integer Width for the carousel's buttons in interface units.
---@field buttonHeight integer Height for the carousel's buttons in interface units.
---@field buttonOffset integer Offset in interface units from the left/right edges applied when positioning the carousel's buttons.
---@field contentMargin ui.Margin (Modifiable Contents) Offsets used to determine the inner content area for this component.
---@field entryText ui.TextData (Read-only) (Modifiable Contents) Text properties used when displaying entry text labels.
---@field buttonSprite ui.SpriteData (Read-only) (Modifiable Contents) Sprite properties used for the carousel's buttons.
---@field backgroundSprite ui.SpriteData (Modifiable Contents) Sprite properties used for the background.
ui.Carousel = {}

---Creates a new carousel on the specified parent.
---
---Warning: Creating a component can fail if there's already a component on that parent with the same category ID and
---dynamic ID, or if those are omitted and the application is unable to generate a valid ID for the component.
---@param parent ui.ComponentCollection Parent component to create this carousel in.
---@param categoryID? integer Category ID used to identify this component. Defaults to the parent's category ID if not specified.
---@param dynamicID? integer Dynamic ID used to identify this component. Defaults to auto-incrementing from the parent's dynamic ID if not specified.
---@return ui.Carousel # The newly created carousel. The caller must set its layout and visual information afterwards.
function ui.Carousel.new(parent, categoryID, dynamicID) end

---Adds an entry to the carousel.
---@param id integer Unique numeric value identifying this entry.
---@param label string Text to display for this entry.
---@return boolean # True if successful, false if an entry with that ID already exists.
---@overload fun(self: ui.Carousel, id: integer, iconSpriteID: integer): boolean
function ui.Carousel:Add(id, label) end

---Removes all entries from the carousel.
function ui.Carousel:Clear() end

---Returns whether or not there's an entry associated with the provided ID.
---@param id integer Numeric value associated with the entry to check.
---@return boolean # True if there is an entry corresponding to the provided ID, false otherwise.
function ui.Carousel:HasEntry(id) end

---Sets whether or not the entry associated with the provided ID is enabled and can be selected.
---@param id integer Numeric value associated with the entry to modify.
---@param enabled boolean Whether or not the entry should be enabled and selectable.
---@return boolean # True if there was an entry corresponding to the provided ID, false otherwise.
function ui.Carousel:SetEntryEnabled(id, enabled) end

---Returns whether or not the entry associated with the provided ID is enabled and selectable.
---@param id integer Numeric value associated with the entry to access.
---@return boolean # True if there was an entry corresponding to the provided ID and it was enabled, false otherwise.
function ui.Carousel:GetEntryEnabled(id) end

---Selects the entry associated with the provided ID, and optionally triggers the corresponding `ONSELECTIONCHANGED`
---events.
---@param id integer Numeric value associated with the entry to select.
---@param triggerEvents? boolean Whether or not to emit `ONSELECTIONCHANGED` events for this change. Defaults to false.
---@return boolean # True if there was an entry corresponding to the provided ID, false otherwise.
function ui.Carousel:Select(id, triggerEvents) end
